{"version": 2, "width": 112, "height": 32, "timestamp": 1754006400, "title": "arv: Archive, Record, Verify", "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/sh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}}
[0.5, "o", "\u001b[1;32marchivist\u001b[0m:\u001b[1;34m~\u001b[0m$ "]
[0.9, "o", "a"]
[0.945, "o", "r"]
[0.99, "o", "v"]
[1.035, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.185, "o", "arv: Archive, Record, Verify. Long-term archiving of what you choose to keep, on discs.\r\n"]
[1.197, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.209, "o", "No archive here yet: arv init FOLDER makes one, at the root of what it describes.\r\n"]
[1.221, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.233, "o", "Start with:\r\n"]
[1.245, "o", "  arv init FOLDER                    an archive (its record: FOLDER/.arv)\r\n"]
[1.257, "o", "  arv collection init FOLDER --code CODE --title TITLE\r\n"]
[1.269, "o", "                                     a folder you keep over time\r\n"]
[1.281, "o", "  arv make FOLDER                    its disc images (--no-ecc to try arv out quickly)\r\n"]
[1.293, "o", "  arv burned --device DRIVE          after burning one: read it back, record the copy\r\n"]
[1.305, "o", "  arv todo                           what is owed: copies, read-backs, checks\r\n"]
[1.317, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.329, "o", "Every command, by group: arv archive, arv record, arv verify, arv home. All of them: arv --help.\r\n"]
[1.341, "o", "In the browser: arv gui. The whole workflow: docs/workflow.md.\r\n"]
